-- title:
--   Local GL₃× GL₁ functional equation for deeply twisted principal series
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a non-zero prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, with residue field of cardinality $q=$ `Ideal.absNorm p.asIdeal`, and write $F=\mathbb{Q}_p$ for the completion at $p$. Let $\lambda_0,\lambda_1,\lambda_2$ be locally constant unitary characters $F^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$, and let $W_2:\mathrm{GL}_3(F)\to\mathbb{C}$ be non-zero and of the form $W_2=$ `coefficientFn` $\Lambda\,f$ for some $f$ in the principal series `principalSeries3` attached to $\lambda$ (locally constant functions invariant under the upper unipotent subgroup and transforming under the diagonal torus by $\prod_i\lambda_i(a_i)$ times $\|a_0\|/\|a_2\|$) and some linear functional $\Lambda$ satisfying $\Lambda(\rho(u(x,y,z))F)=\psi_p^{-1}(x+y)\Lambda(F)$, where $\psi_p$ is the standard local additive character. Let $\chi$ be a unitary character of $F^\times$ and $d\ge 1$ be such that each $\lambda_i\chi^{-1}$ is trivial on the units $u$ with $\|u\|=1$ and $\|u-1\|\le q^{-d}$, and assume that the cyclic subspace generated by $W_2$ under right translation contains a non-zero $W'$ for which $g\mapsto\chi(\det g)^{-1}W'(g)$ is invariant under right translation by those $k$ in the maximal compact `localMaximalCompact3` whose entries are congruent to those of $1$ modulo valuation $\le q^{-d}$. Let $\xi$ be a unitary character of $F^\times$ of exact conductor exponent $B$ (trivial on the $B$-th principal units, non-trivial on the $m$-th for every $m<B$) with $2d+1\le B$. Put $W_3(g)=\xi(\det g)\chi(\det g)^{-1}W_2(g)$. Then there is $\varepsilon\neq 0$ such that for every $g\in\mathrm{GL}_3(F)$ there are a function $P:\mathbb{C}\to\mathbb{C}$ and reals $\sigma_0,\sigma_1$ with: $P$ is rational in $q^{-s}$, in the sense that $P(s)R(q^{-s})=Q(q^{-s})q^{ms}$ for all $s$, for some polynomials $Q,R$ over $\mathbb{C}$ with $R\neq 0$ and some $m\in\mathbb{N}$; the $(3,0)$ integrand $a\mapsto W_3(\iota(\mathrm{diag}(a,1))g)\,\|a\|^{s-1}$ is integrable for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_0$ with respect to the multiplicative measure obtained from the self-dual Haar measure at $p$, and $\zeta_{3,0}(W_3,\mathbf 1,s,g)=P(s)$ there; the corresponding $(3,1)$ integrand for the dual Whittaker function $g\mapsto W_3(w_{\mathrm{long}}\,{}^t g^{-1})$ at the point $w'\,{}^tg^{-1}$ is integrable for $\mathrm{Re}\,s>\sigma_1$; and for $\mathrm{Re}(1-s)>\sigma_1$ one has $\widetilde\zeta_{3,1}(W_3,\mathbf 1,1-s,g)=\varepsilon\,q^{3B(1/2-s)}P(s)$. Both zeta integrals are taken against the trivial character of $F^\times$, and no Euler factors occur on either side.
--
--   This is the local $GL_3\times GL_1$ functional equation at the trivial character for a principal-series Whittaker function twisted by a highly ramified character, in the stability range $B\ge 2d+1$: the Euler factors on both sides are trivial and the epsilon factor reduces to a constant times $q^{3B(1/2-s)}$. It supplies the local input at a ramified place for the $GL_3$ converse theorem used in the Langlands–Tunnell step.
